>> title: Corn Chowder
>> category: Soups
>> tags: corn, bacon, potatoes, summer, stovetop
>> servings: 6
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: render in a Dutch oven
>> step.2: sweat 6 min
>> step.3: stir in flour 2 min
>> step.4: simmer 15 min
>> step.5: purée in a blender
>> step.6: cook 5 min, season

Render @bacon{4%slices}(chopped) in a #Dutch oven{} until crisp.

Sweat @&(~1)bacon{} in its fat for ~{6%min} with @yellow onion{1%large} and @celery{2%ribs}.

Cook @&(~1)base{} for ~{2%min} with @all-purpose flour{3%Tbs}(25 g).

Simmer @&(~1)base{} for ~{15%min} with @Yukon Gold potatoes{1%lb}(450 g; cubed), @chicken stock{4%cups}(950 mL), and @thyme{2%sprigs}.

Purée @corn kernels{1 1/2%cups}(225 g; from about 2 ears) with @whole milk{2%cups}(480 mL) in a #blender{} until smooth.

Cook @&(~2)chowder{} for ~{5%min} with @&(~1)corn milk{} and @corn kernels{2 1/2%cups}(375 g; from about 3 ears), then season with @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.
